    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-1-sec-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 Application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-1-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments made by items 1 to 5 of this Schedule apply in relation\nto corrupt conduct, whether engaged in before or after the\ncommencement of the Law Enforcement Integrity Commissioner Act\n2006.\n(2)\nHowever, the requirement for the Chief Executive Officer of Customs\nto notify a corruption issue to the Integrity Commissioner under that\nAct only applies on and after this item commences.\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, the amendments made by items 1 to 5 apply in relation\nto corrupt conduct even if the conduct was engaged in at a time when\nCustoms was known as the Australian Customs Service.\n(4)\nIn this item:\ncorrupt conduct has the same meaning as in the Law Enforcement\nIntegrity Commissioner Act 2006.\ncorruption issue has the same meaning as in the Law Enforcement\nIntegrity Commissioner Act 2006.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nProceeds of crime amendments  Schedule 2\nResponsible authorities for proceeds of crime: the DPP and the AFP  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011          5",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe amendments made by items 1 to 5 of this Schedule apply in relation\nto corrupt conduct, whether engaged in before or after the\ncommencement of the Law Enforcement Integrity Commissioner Act\n2006.\n(2)\nHowever, the requirement for the Chief Executive Officer of Customs\nto notify a corruption issue to the Integrity Commissioner under that\nAct only applies on and after this item commences.\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, the amendments made by items 1 to 5 apply in relation\nto corrupt conduct even if the conduct was engaged in at a time when\nCustoms was known as the Australian Customs Service.\n(4)\nIn this item:\ncorrupt conduct has the same meaning as in the Law Enforcement\nIntegrity Commissioner Act 2006.\ncorruption issue has the same meaning as in the Law Enforcement\nIntegrity Commissioner Act 2006.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nProceeds of crime amendments  Schedule 2\nResponsible authorities for proceeds of crime: the DPP and the AFP  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011          5",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-1-sec-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-1-sec-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d562b0b47e9b2109524f6621b4711769cf770ce8ef285eb7f8191fc78f8daa61",
      "skos:note": "Amendments apply in relation to corrupt conduct, regardless of when it was engaged in."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-1-sec-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 Application",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments made by items 1 to 5 of this Schedule apply in relation\nto corrupt conduct, whether engaged in before or after the\ncommencement of the Law Enforcement Integrity Commissioner Act\n2006.\n(2)\nHowever, the requirement for the Chief Executive Officer of Customs\nto notify a corruption issue to the Integrity Commissioner under that\nAct only applies on and after this item commences.\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, the amendments made by items 1 to 5 apply in relation\nto corrupt conduct even if the conduct was engaged in at a time when\nCustoms was known as the Australian Customs Service.\n(4)\nIn this item:\ncorrupt conduct has the same meaning as in the Law Enforcement\nIntegrity Commissioner Act 2006.\ncorruption issue has the same meaning as in the Law Enforcement\nIntegrity Commissioner Act 2006.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nProceeds of crime amendments  Schedule 2\nResponsible authorities for proceeds of crime: the DPP and the AFP  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011          5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-1-sec-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-1-sec-6"
      },
