    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-1-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 At the end of section 69C",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-1-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(3) The Commissioner may, in writing, delegate to the Deputy\nCommissioner or a senior executive AFP employee all or any of\nthe Commissioner’s powers, functions or duties as a proceeds of\ncrime authority under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 or any other\nAct.\nNote:\nAs a proceeds of crime authority, the Commissioner may conduct\nproceedings under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, and has related\npowers, functions and duties under that Act and other Acts (see the\ndefinitions of proceeds of crime authority and responsible authority\nin section 338 of that Act).",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(3) The Commissioner may, in writing, delegate to the Deputy\nCommissioner or a senior executive AFP employee all or any of\nthe Commissioner’s powers, functions or duties as a proceeds of\ncrime authority under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 or any other\nAct.\nNote:\nAs a proceeds of crime authority, the Commissioner may conduct\nproceedings under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, and has related\npowers, functions and duties under that Act and other Acts (see the\ndefinitions of proceeds of crime authority and responsible authority\nin section 338 of that Act).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-1-5-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6cfc72e43dda61c48a64f9238282f41e8cdf1d202980dafbe342f3e81a6da600",
      "skos:note": "Commissioner may delegate powers to Deputy Commissioner or senior executive AFP employee."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-1-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 At the end of section 69C",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(3) The Commissioner may, in writing, delegate to the Deputy\nCommissioner or a senior executive AFP employee all or any of\nthe Commissioner’s powers, functions or duties as a proceeds of\ncrime authority under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 or any other\nAct.\nNote:\nAs a proceeds of crime authority, the Commissioner may conduct\nproceedings under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, and has related\npowers, functions and duties under that Act and other Acts (see the\ndefinitions of proceeds of crime authority and responsible authority\nin section 338 of that Act)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-1-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-1-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-2-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 Application of amendment—the Australian Federal Police",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-2-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "Act 1979\n(1)\nThe amendment of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979 made by\nitem 1 of this Schedule applies as set out in this item.\n(2)\nThe amendment applies in relation to the Commissioner’s powers,\nfunctions or duties as a proceeds of crime authority in relation to orders\n(or applications or proceedings for orders) under the Proceeds of Crime\nAct 2002 made or (in the case of proceedings) started before, at or after\nthe commencement of item 1.\n(3)\nThe amendments apply under subitem (2) of this item regardless of\nwhether the conduct giving rise to those orders (or applications or\nproceedings for orders) occurred, or is suspected to have occurred,\nbefore, at or after the commencement of item 1.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nSchedule 2  Proceeds of crime amendments",
      "skos:definition": "Act 1979\n(1)\nThe amendment of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979 made by\nitem 1 of this Schedule applies as set out in this item.\n(2)\nThe amendment applies in relation to the Commissioner’s powers,\nfunctions or duties as a proceeds of crime authority in relation to orders\n(or applications or proceedings for orders) under the Proceeds of Crime\nAct 2002 made or (in the case of proceedings) started before, at or after\nthe commencement of item 1.\n(3)\nThe amendments apply under subitem (2) of this item regardless of\nwhether the conduct giving rise to those orders (or applications or\nproceedings for orders) occurred, or is suspected to have occurred,\nbefore, at or after the commencement of item 1.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nSchedule 2  Proceeds of crime amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-2-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f2579f4261840c6c5920184c7f2c82218c7167343efbad0bc9c034edb042ce3d",
      "skos:note": "Amendment application to Commissioner's powers, functions or duties as a proceeds of crime authority"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-2-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 Application of amendment—the Australian Federal Police",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "Act 1979\n(1)\nThe amendment of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979 made by\nitem 1 of this Schedule applies as set out in this item.\n(2)\nThe amendment applies in relation to the Commissioner’s powers,\nfunctions or duties as a proceeds of crime authority in relation to orders\n(or applications or proceedings for orders) under the Proceeds of Crime\nAct 2002 made or (in the case of proceedings) started before, at or after\nthe commencement of item 1.\n(3)\nThe amendments apply under subitem (2) of this item regardless of\nwhether the conduct giving rise to those orders (or applications or\nproceedings for orders) occurred, or is suspected to have occurred,\nbefore, at or after the commencement of item 1.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nSchedule 2  Proceeds of crime amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-2-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
