      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Diffuses",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Transfer of responsibility diffuses to the transferee authority.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The responsible authority is referred to in this Act as...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the transferor authority may transfer responsibility for..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-315b-ss-1-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recognizes",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Transfer of responsibility recognizes the role of the transferee authority.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The proceeds of crime authority is the Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police, or the DPP.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...or to which responsibility is transferred under this section."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-315b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "315B(2) Transfer of responsibility for principal orders and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-315b-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The transferee authority must give a written notice of transfer of\nresponsibility for an application for a *principal order, or for a\nprincipal order, to:\n\n(a) in the case of a transfer of responsibility for an application\nfor a principal order:\n\n(i) the court before which proceedings on the application\nare being heard (or are to be heard); and\n\n(ii) each party (if any) to those proceedings; and\n\n(iii) any court in which proceedings related to the\napplication are being heard, or are to be heard, if the\ntransferee authority considers it appropriate; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nProceeds of crime amendments  Schedule 2\nResponsible authorities for proceeds of crime: the DPP and the AFP  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011          7\n\n(iv) any person to whom notice of the application has been\ngiven; and\n\n(v) the Family Court of Australia, if an application has been\nmade to that court by a *proceeds of crime authority for\na stay of proceedings because of the application for the\nprincipal order, or that court has given notice to a\nproceeds of crime authority of a stay having been\ngranted; or\n\n(b) in the case of a transfer of responsibility for a principal order:\n\n(i) the court that made the order; and\n\n(ii) each party (if any) to the proceedings in that court on\nthe application for the order; and\n\n(iii) any court in which proceedings related to the order are\nbeing heard, or are to be heard, if the transferee\nauthority considers it appropriate; and\n\n(iv) any person to whom notice of the order, or of the\napplication for the order, has been given; and\n\n(v) the Family Court of Australia, if an application has been\nmade to that court by a proceeds of crime authority for a\nstay of proceedings because of the order or the\napplication for the order, or that court has given notice\nto a proceeds of crime authority of a stay having been\ngranted.\nNote:\nNotice is not required to be given in the circumstances mentioned in\nsubsection (4).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The transferee authority must give a written notice of transfer of\nresponsibility for an application for a *principal order, or for a\nprincipal order, to:\n\n(a) in the case of a transfer of responsibility for an application\nfor a principal order:\n\n(i) the court before which proceedings on the application\nare being heard (or are to be heard); and\n\n(ii) each party (if any) to those proceedings; and\n\n(iii) any court in which proceedings related to the\napplication are being heard, or are to be heard, if the\ntransferee authority considers it appropriate; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nProceeds of crime amendments  Schedule 2\nResponsible authorities for proceeds of crime: the DPP and the AFP  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011          7\n\n(iv) any person to whom notice of the application has been\ngiven; and\n\n(v) the Family Court of Australia, if an application has been\nmade to that court by a *proceeds of crime authority for\na stay of proceedings because of the application for the\nprincipal order, or that court has given notice to a\nproceeds of crime authority of a stay having been\ngranted; or\n\n(b) in the case of a transfer of responsibility for a principal order:\n\n(i) the court that made the order; and\n\n(ii) each party (if any) to the proceedings in that court on\nthe application for the order; and\n\n(iii) any court in which proceedings related to the order are\nbeing heard, or are to be heard, if the transferee\nauthority considers it appropriate; and\n\n(iv) any person to whom notice of the order, or of the\napplication for the order, has been given; and\n\n(v) the Family Court of Australia, if an application has been\nmade to that court by a proceeds of crime authority for a\nstay of proceedings because of the order or the\napplication for the order, or that court has given notice\nto a proceeds of crime authority of a stay having been\ngranted.\nNote:\nNotice is not required to be given in the circumstances mentioned in\nsubsection (4).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-315b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-315b-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-315b-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9a7ed156b93a3a3748ab351c1db1f0ccb36d46d7bcac698bf9ae7312007cad1f",
      "skos:note": "Transfer notice to be given to specified parties upon transfer of responsibility for principal orders."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-315b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "315B(2) Transfer of responsibility for principal orders and",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The transferee authority must give a written notice of transfer of\nresponsibility for an application for a *principal order, or for a\nprincipal order, to:\n\n(a) in the case of a transfer of responsibility for an application\nfor a principal order:\n\n(i) the court before which proceedings on the application\nare being heard (or are to be heard); and\n\n(ii) each party (if any) to those proceedings; and\n\n(iii) any court in which proceedings related to the\napplication are being heard, or are to be heard, if the\ntransferee authority considers it appropriate; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nProceeds of crime amendments  Schedule 2\nResponsible authorities for proceeds of crime: the DPP and the AFP  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011          7\n\n(iv) any person to whom notice of the application has been\ngiven; and\n\n(v) the Family Court of Australia, if an application has been\nmade to that court by a *proceeds of crime authority for\na stay of proceedings because of the application for the\nprincipal order, or that court has given notice to a\nproceeds of crime authority of a stay having been\ngranted; or\n\n(b) in the case of a transfer of responsibility for a principal order:\n\n(i) the court that made the order; and\n\n(ii) each party (if any) to the proceedings in that court on\nthe application for the order; and\n\n(iii) any court in which proceedings related to the order are\nbeing heard, or are to be heard, if the transferee\nauthority considers it appropriate; and\n\n(iv) any person to whom notice of the order, or of the\napplication for the order, has been given; and\n\n(v) the Family Court of Australia, if an application has been\nmade to that court by a proceeds of crime authority for a\nstay of proceedings because of the order or the\napplication for the order, or that court has given notice\nto a proceeds of crime authority of a stay having been\ngranted.\nNote:\nNotice is not required to be given in the circumstances mentioned in\nsubsection (4)."
    },
    {
