    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-150",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "150 Application of amendments—the Bankruptcy Act 1966",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-150"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments of the Bankruptcy Act 1966 made by items 142 to 149\nof this Schedule apply as set out in this item.\n(2)\nThe amendments apply in relation to proceeds of crime orders (or\napplications, proceedings or pending proceedings for proceeds of crime\norders), or proceedings under the Bankruptcy Act 1966, made or (in the\ncase of proceedings) started before, at or after the commencement of\nthose items.\n(3)\nThe amendments apply under subitem (2) of this item regardless of\nwhether the conduct giving rise to those orders (or applications or\nproceedings for orders) occurred, or is suspected to have occurred,\nbefore, at or after the commencement of those items.\nCrimes Act 1914",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe amendments of the Bankruptcy Act 1966 made by items 142 to 149\nof this Schedule apply as set out in this item.\n(2)\nThe amendments apply in relation to proceeds of crime orders (or\napplications, proceedings or pending proceedings for proceeds of crime\norders), or proceedings under the Bankruptcy Act 1966, made or (in the\ncase of proceedings) started before, at or after the commencement of\nthose items.\n(3)\nThe amendments apply under subitem (2) of this item regardless of\nwhether the conduct giving rise to those orders (or applications or\nproceedings for orders) occurred, or is suspected to have occurred,\nbefore, at or after the commencement of those items.\nCrimes Act 1914",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-150-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3890b63ab947d2b2ff8e6107c37bc7e8c65bd5eb5cb90f8313c25d827736e6d6",
      "skos:note": "Application of amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-150",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "150 Application of amendments—the Bankruptcy Act 1966",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments of the Bankruptcy Act 1966 made by items 142 to 149\nof this Schedule apply as set out in this item.\n(2)\nThe amendments apply in relation to proceeds of crime orders (or\napplications, proceedings or pending proceedings for proceeds of crime\norders), or proceedings under the Bankruptcy Act 1966, made or (in the\ncase of proceedings) started before, at or after the commencement of\nthose items.\n(3)\nThe amendments apply under subitem (2) of this item regardless of\nwhether the conduct giving rise to those orders (or applications or\nproceedings for orders) occurred, or is suspected to have occurred,\nbefore, at or after the commencement of those items.\nCrimes Act 1914"
    },
