    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-26-2-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26(4) Crimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-26-2-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(4) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), in relation to a provision of\nthis Act, proceeds of crime authority means a person or body\nprescribed by the regulations to be the proceeds of crime authority\nfor that provision in relation to:\n\n(a) a class of proceeds of crime order, under the relevant State or\nTerritory proceeds of crime law, prescribed by the\nregulations, that includes the relevant proceeds of crime\norder; or\n\n(b) a class of forfeiture application, under the relevant State or\nTerritory proceeds of crime law, prescribed by the\nregulations, that includes the relevant forfeiture application.\nNote:\nThe regulations may prescribe a proceeds of crime authority in\nrelation to a proceeds of crime order under a State or Territory\nproceeds of crime law by reference to any matter, including (for\nexample) by reference to who applied for the order.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), in relation to a provision of\nthis Act, proceeds of crime authority means a person or body\nprescribed by the regulations to be the proceeds of crime authority\nfor that provision in relation to:\n\n(a) a class of proceeds of crime order, under the relevant State or\nTerritory proceeds of crime law, prescribed by the\nregulations, that includes the relevant proceeds of crime\norder; or\n\n(b) a class of forfeiture application, under the relevant State or\nTerritory proceeds of crime law, prescribed by the\nregulations, that includes the relevant forfeiture application.\nNote:\nThe regulations may prescribe a proceeds of crime authority in\nrelation to a proceeds of crime order under a State or Territory\nproceeds of crime law by reference to any matter, including (for\nexample) by reference to who applied for the order.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-26-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-26-2-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-26-2-ss-4-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-26-2-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "83a940f9e41f55cb959b488a2deeae6db1dc603775760a5f56f8cefab6ea74f4",
      "skos:note": "Defines proceeds of crime authority for a provision in relation to a class of proceeds of crime order or forfeiture application."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-26-2-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26(4) Crimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(4) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), in relation to a provision of\nthis Act, proceeds of crime authority means a person or body\nprescribed by the regulations to be the proceeds of crime authority\nfor that provision in relation to:\n\n(a) a class of proceeds of crime order, under the relevant State or\nTerritory proceeds of crime law, prescribed by the\nregulations, that includes the relevant proceeds of crime\norder; or\n\n(b) a class of forfeiture application, under the relevant State or\nTerritory proceeds of crime law, prescribed by the\nregulations, that includes the relevant forfeiture application.\nNote:\nThe regulations may prescribe a proceeds of crime authority in\nrelation to a proceeds of crime order under a State or Territory\nproceeds of crime law by reference to any matter, including (for\nexample) by reference to who applied for the order."
    },
