    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-196",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "196 At the end of subsection 25A(2)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-196"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nNote:\nUnder that Act, the responsible authority is the Commissioner of the\nAustralian Federal Police or the Director of Public Prosecutions (see\nthe definitions of responsible authority and proceeds of crime\nauthority in section 338 of that Act). Responsibility can be transferred\nbetween these authorities (see section 315B of that Act).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nProceeds of crime amendments  Schedule 2\nResponsible authorities for proceeds of crime: the DPP and the AFP  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011          31",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\nNote:\nUnder that Act, the responsible authority is the Commissioner of the\nAustralian Federal Police or the Director of Public Prosecutions (see\nthe definitions of responsible authority and proceeds of crime\nauthority in section 338 of that Act). Responsibility can be transferred\nbetween these authorities (see section 315B of that Act).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nProceeds of crime amendments  Schedule 2\nResponsible authorities for proceeds of crime: the DPP and the AFP  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011          31",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-196-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "557be39a5c60b66ef02e561ffc4ee11dfd9c2939c4595854a92c0568f9dbfbd0",
      "skos:note": "Defines responsible authorities for proceeds of crime"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-196",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "196 At the end of subsection 25A(2)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nNote:\nUnder that Act, the responsible authority is the Commissioner of the\nAustralian Federal Police or the Director of Public Prosecutions (see\nthe definitions of responsible authority and proceeds of crime\nauthority in section 338 of that Act). Responsibility can be transferred\nbetween these authorities (see section 315B of that Act).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nProceeds of crime amendments  Schedule 2\nResponsible authorities for proceeds of crime: the DPP and the AFP  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011          31"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-196-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-196"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-197",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "197 Application of amendments—the Foreign Evidence Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-197"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf, p.35",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments of the Foreign Evidence Act 1994 made by items 195\nand 196 of this Schedule apply as set out in this item.\n(2)\nThe amendments apply in relation to proceedings under the Proceeds of\nCrime Act 2002 started before, at or after the commencement of those\nitems.\n(3)\nThe amendments apply under subitem (2) of this item regardless of\nwhether the conduct giving rise to those proceedings occurred, or is\nsuspected to have occurred, before, at or after the commencement of\nthose items.\nInternational Criminal Court Act 2002",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe amendments of the Foreign Evidence Act 1994 made by items 195\nand 196 of this Schedule apply as set out in this item.\n(2)\nThe amendments apply in relation to proceedings under the Proceeds of\nCrime Act 2002 started before, at or after the commencement of those\nitems.\n(3)\nThe amendments apply under subitem (2) of this item regardless of\nwhether the conduct giving rise to those proceedings occurred, or is\nsuspected to have occurred, before, at or after the commencement of\nthose items.\nInternational Criminal Court Act 2002",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-197-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "07a520650348a7982af60d5df228afbb1580cb1a4b6404f91a34e1e257aa0e4e",
      "skos:note": "Application of amendments made by items 195 and 196 of this Schedule"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-197",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "197 Application of amendments—the Foreign Evidence Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 35,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments of the Foreign Evidence Act 1994 made by items 195\nand 196 of this Schedule apply as set out in this item.\n(2)\nThe amendments apply in relation to proceedings under the Proceeds of\nCrime Act 2002 started before, at or after the commencement of those\nitems.\n(3)\nThe amendments apply under subitem (2) of this item regardless of\nwhether the conduct giving rise to those proceedings occurred, or is\nsuspected to have occurred, before, at or after the commencement of\nthose items.\nInternational Criminal Court Act 2002"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-197-norm",
