    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-209",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "209 Application of amendments—the International Criminal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-209"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "Court Act 2002\n(1)\nThe amendments of the International Criminal Court Act 2002 made by\nitems 198 to 208 of this Schedule apply as set out in this item.\n(2)\nThe amendments apply in relation to requests by the ICC (within the\nmeaning of that Act) to the Attorney-General under that Act made\nbefore, at or after the commencement of those items.\n(3)\nThe amendments apply under subitem (2) of this item regardless of\nwhether the conduct giving rise to those requests occurred, or is\nsuspected to have occurred, before, at or after the commencement of\nthose items.\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995",
      "skos:definition": "Court Act 2002\n(1)\nThe amendments of the International Criminal Court Act 2002 made by\nitems 198 to 208 of this Schedule apply as set out in this item.\n(2)\nThe amendments apply in relation to requests by the ICC (within the\nmeaning of that Act) to the Attorney-General under that Act made\nbefore, at or after the commencement of those items.\n(3)\nThe amendments apply under subitem (2) of this item regardless of\nwhether the conduct giving rise to those requests occurred, or is\nsuspected to have occurred, before, at or after the commencement of\nthose items.\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-209-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9531bc0ad490f371fd0c986e602c59429c1ec4137c2d14e1098017d29b673bfa",
      "skos:note": "Application of amendments—the International Criminal Court Act 2002"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-209",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "209 Application of amendments—the International Criminal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "Court Act 2002\n(1)\nThe amendments of the International Criminal Court Act 2002 made by\nitems 198 to 208 of this Schedule apply as set out in this item.\n(2)\nThe amendments apply in relation to requests by the ICC (within the\nmeaning of that Act) to the Attorney-General under that Act made\nbefore, at or after the commencement of those items.\n(3)\nThe amendments apply under subitem (2) of this item regardless of\nwhether the conduct giving rise to those requests occurred, or is\nsuspected to have occurred, before, at or after the commencement of\nthose items.\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-209-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-209"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-210",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "210 Section 4",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-210"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nproceeds of crime authority has the same meaning as in the\nProceeds of Crime Act 2002.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nProceeds of crime amendments  Schedule 2\nResponsible authorities for proceeds of crime: the DPP and the AFP  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011          33\nNote:\nUnder that Act, the proceeds of crime authority is either the\nCommissioner of the Australian Federal Police or the Director of\nPublic Prosecutions (see the definition of proceeds of crime authority\nin section 338 of that Act).",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\nproceeds of crime authority has the same meaning as in the\nProceeds of Crime Act 2002.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nProceeds of crime amendments  Schedule 2\nResponsible authorities for proceeds of crime: the DPP and the AFP  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011          33\nNote:\nUnder that Act, the proceeds of crime authority is either the\nCommissioner of the Australian Federal Police or the Director of\nPublic Prosecutions (see the definition of proceeds of crime authority\nin section 338 of that Act).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-210-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-210-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5fae416f5d41cba37728de8a391f5c1d344535fdc835ac9d0118e6306cbf2bd2",
      "skos:note": "Defines the proceeds of crime authority"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-210",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "210 Section 4",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nproceeds of crime authority has the same meaning as in the\nProceeds of Crime Act 2002.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nProceeds of crime amendments  Schedule 2\nResponsible authorities for proceeds of crime: the DPP and the AFP  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment Act (No. 2) 2011          33\nNote:\nUnder that Act, the proceeds of crime authority is either the\nCommissioner of the Australian Federal Police or the Director of\nPublic Prosecutions (see the definition of proceeds of crime authority\nin section 338 of that Act)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-210-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-210"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
