    {
      "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-242",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "242 Application of amendments—the Trade Marks Act 1995",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-242"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments of the Trade Marks Act 1995 made by items 240 and\n241 of this Schedule apply as set out in this item.\n(2)\nSubject to subitem (3) of this item, the amendment made by item 240\napplies in relation to proceedings for the prosecution of a person in\nrespect of an indictable offence against Part 14 of that Act instituted\nbefore, at or after the commencement of that item.\n(3)\nHowever, if Divisions 1 and 2 of Part II of the Proceeds of Crime Act\n1987 apply immediately before the commencement of items 240 and\n241 of this Schedule in relation to proceedings for the prosecution of a\nperson in respect of an indictable offence against Part 14 of the Trade\nMarks Act 1995 instituted before that commencement, the Divisions\ncontinue to apply in relation to the proceedings as if the amendments\nmade by those items had not been made.\n(4)\nThe amendment made by item 241 of this Schedule applies in relation\nto proceedings for the prosecution of a person in respect of an indictable\noffence against Part 14 of the Trade Marks Act 1995 instituted at or\nafter the commencement of that item.\n(5)\nThe amendments apply under subitems (2) and (4) of this item\nregardless of whether the conduct giving rise to those proceedings\noccurred, or is suspected to have occurred, before, at or after the\ncommencement of items 240 and 241.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nSchedule 2  Proceeds of crime amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe amendments of the Trade Marks Act 1995 made by items 240 and\n241 of this Schedule apply as set out in this item.\n(2)\nSubject to subitem (3) of this item, the amendment made by item 240\napplies in relation to proceedings for the prosecution of a person in\nrespect of an indictable offence against Part 14 of that Act instituted\nbefore, at or after the commencement of that item.\n(3)\nHowever, if Divisions 1 and 2 of Part II of the Proceeds of Crime Act\n1987 apply immediately before the commencement of items 240 and\n241 of this Schedule in relation to proceedings for the prosecution of a\nperson in respect of an indictable offence against Part 14 of the Trade\nMarks Act 1995 instituted before that commencement, the Divisions\ncontinue to apply in relation to the proceedings as if the amendments\nmade by those items had not been made.\n(4)\nThe amendment made by item 241 of this Schedule applies in relation\nto proceedings for the prosecution of a person in respect of an indictable\noffence against Part 14 of the Trade Marks Act 1995 instituted at or\nafter the commencement of that item.\n(5)\nThe amendments apply under subitems (2) and (4) of this item\nregardless of whether the conduct giving rise to those proceedings\noccurred, or is suspected to have occurred, before, at or after the\ncommencement of items 240 and 241.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nSchedule 2  Proceeds of crime amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-242-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9f44fd90d7ff24d24687466ced05cdf511af9b11627347868d984fc73ccd1d0a",
      "skos:note": "Application of amendments—the Trade Marks Act 1995"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-242",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "242 Application of amendments—the Trade Marks Act 1995",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 41,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments of the Trade Marks Act 1995 made by items 240 and\n241 of this Schedule apply as set out in this item.\n(2)\nSubject to subitem (3) of this item, the amendment made by item 240\napplies in relation to proceedings for the prosecution of a person in\nrespect of an indictable offence against Part 14 of that Act instituted\nbefore, at or after the commencement of that item.\n(3)\nHowever, if Divisions 1 and 2 of Part II of the Proceeds of Crime Act\n1987 apply immediately before the commencement of items 240 and\n241 of this Schedule in relation to proceedings for the prosecution of a\nperson in respect of an indictable offence against Part 14 of the Trade\nMarks Act 1995 instituted before that commencement, the Divisions\ncontinue to apply in relation to the proceedings as if the amendments\nmade by those items had not been made.\n(4)\nThe amendment made by item 241 of this Schedule applies in relation\nto proceedings for the prosecution of a person in respect of an indictable\noffence against Part 14 of the Trade Marks Act 1995 instituted at or\nafter the commencement of that item.\n(5)\nThe amendments apply under subitems (2) and (4) of this item\nregardless of whether the conduct giving rise to those proceedings\noccurred, or is suspected to have occurred, before, at or after the\ncommencement of items 240 and 241.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00859\n\nSchedule 2  Proceeds of crime amendments"
    },
