      "dc:source": "an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the.pdf, p.42",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nTax paid after application for order is made\n\n(1A) The court may, if it considers that it is in the interests of justice to\ndo so, reduce the *penalty amount under a *pecuniary penalty order\nagainst a person by an amount that, in the court’s opinion,\nrepresents the extent to which tax that the person has paid at or\nafter the time the application for the order is made is attributable to\nthe *benefits to which the order relates.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\nTax paid after application for order is made\n\n(1A) The court may, if it considers that it is in the interests of justice to\ndo so, reduce the *penalty amount under a *pecuniary penalty order\nagainst a person by an amount that, in the court’s opinion,\nrepresents the extent to which tax that the person has paid at or\nafter the time the application for the order is made is attributable to\nthe *benefits to which the order relates.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-244-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the-sch-2-sec-244-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6294f8cfead1ecb83390ea380796353f5b212dca1502163eccfe6fd1ee44bb90",
      "skos:note": "Court may reduce penalty amount in interest of justice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/an-act-to-amend-various-acts-relating-to-the-enforcement-of-the#sch-2-sec-244",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "244 After subsection 131(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 42,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nTax paid after application for order is made\n\n(1A) The court may, if it considers that it is in the interests of justice to\ndo so, reduce the *penalty amount under a *pecuniary penalty order\nagainst a person by an amount that, in the court’s opinion,\nrepresents the extent to which tax that the person has paid at or\nafter the time the application for the order is made is attributable to\nthe *benefits to which the order relates."
    },
